      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: Could we just have a single Value property with type `string` here instead of having two properties which cover the same data. Since we format structs to a string before returning from `reflectionValue`, we could do the same thing for slices with `fmt.Sprintf(\"[%s]\", strings.Join(vals, \", \"))` inside the `reflectionValue` function.\n\nI might just be missing the use case for the `Values` property though.",
