      "side": 1,
      "message": "The use case for structs in a list is quite rare (afaik, Dists is only the property that uses a slice of structs), whereas slices of strings are quite common.\n\nI separated this into Values for slices as I think querying on elements of a slice will be a very common use case. As such\n1. needing to split a string to query on the values each time would be frustrating\n2. potentially more errorprone (e.g. splitting on `\u0027,\u0027` rather than `\u0027, \u0027`, the results may have slightly incorrect results)\n\nwdyt?",
